# Which models/articles/judges to run — tracked in git (unlike
# /etc/eval-harness.env, which holds secrets and is never committed).
# Edit this file, commit, `git pull` on the droplet, then
# `sudo systemctl restart eval-harness` to pick it up. Already-completed
# (model, article) pairs are cached and won't be redone.
#
# Same flags as `python3 scripts/eval_harness.py run` locally — see
# eval/README.md. Split on whitespace (at use, in run.sh), so no argument
# here can contain a space (none of these flags need one).
#
# MUST stay double-quoted: this file is bash-`source`d (not parsed by
# systemd's more forgiving EnvironmentFile format), so an unquoted value
# with spaces is read as "set RUN_ARGS=--models, then run the next word as
# a command" — bash tries to execute the first model slug as a program and
# fails with "No such file or directory".
# qwen3-235b-a22b dropped: 10/10 gen errors in do-batch-1 (OpenRouter 404 —
# "No endpoints available matching your guardrail restrictions and data
# policy"), meaning its providers don't meet the account's ZDR/no-training
# policy. Re-add only after confirming it shows up in the account's
# ZDR-filtered model list.
RUN_ARGS="--models qwen/qwen3-30b-a3b google/gemma-3-27b-it google/gemma-4-26b-a4b-it qwen/qwen3.8-27 google/gemini-3.7-flash --judges opus gpt --run-id do-batch-2"
